All other cases are called less-than-supervised. Unsupervised learning proceeds without any labels. Such approaches are typically designed to learn implicitly or explicitly the data probability density p⁡(x)p(x). This can be useful for various tasks including generative modeling and anomaly detection. Three standard approaches to unsupervised deep learning include Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs) [Goodfellow et al. 2014](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2112.03769#bib.bib31); [Creswell et al. 2018](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2112.03769#bib.bib32), (Variational) Autoencoders (VAEs) [Kingma and Welling 2014](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2112.03769#bib.bib33); [Kingma and Welling 2019](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2112.03769#bib.bib34), and Normalizing Flows (NFs) [Rezende and Mohamed 2015](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2112.03769#bib.bib35); [Kobyzev et al. 2020](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2112.03769#bib.bib36), first studied in HEP in Refs. [de Oliveira et al. 2017](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2112.03769#bib.bib37); [Mustafa et al. 2019](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2112.03769#bib.bib38), [ATL 2018a](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2112.03769#bib.bib39); [Hajer et al. 2020](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2112.03769#bib.bib40); [Farina et al. 2020](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2112.03769#bib.bib41); [Heimel et al. 2019](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2112.03769#bib.bib42), and [Albergo et al. 2019](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2112.03769#bib.bib43); [Gao et al. 2020a](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2112.03769#bib.bib44); [Gao et al. 2020b](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2112.03769#bib.bib45); [Bothmann et al. 2020](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2112.03769#bib.bib46); [Nachman and Shih 2020](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2112.03769#bib.bib47), respectively. Each44 4 In the case of autoencoders, this is only true for variational architectures. of these methods learns to map a random variable Z