Most less-than-supervised searches in HEP differ from the typical anomaly detection setting in industry because pSMp\_{\text{SM}} is usually not zero. No single event can be labeled as signal with certainty and so HEP often targets group or collective anomalies as opposed to point or off-manifold anomalies that are common elsewhere. Many examples of less-than-supervised methods can be additionally found in the recent LHC Olympics and Dark Machines community challenge reports [Kasieczka et al. 2021](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2112.03769#bib.bib126); [Aarrestad et al. 2021a](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2112.03769#bib.bib127).

